Assume Countable Choice. Fix $\theta\in(0,\pi/2)$ and put $S_\theta:=\{z\in\mathbb C\setminus\{0\}:|\arg z|<\theta\}$. For $z\in S_\theta$ and $x\in\mathbb R^n$ define the **complex-time heat kernel**
$$\Gamma_z(x):=(4\pi z)^{-n/2}\exp\Bigl(-\frac{|x|^2}{4z}\Bigr),$$
where $(4\pi z)^{-n/2}:=\exp\bigl(-\frac n2\operatorname{Log}(4\pi z)\bigr)$ with the principal logarithm, legitimate because $\operatorname{Re}(4\pi z)>0$. Then:

(i) $\Gamma_z\in C^\infty(\mathbb R^n)\cap L^1(\mathbb R^n)$ and $\int_{\mathbb R^n}\Gamma_z(x)\,dx=1$;

(ii) for every $\sigma\in(0,\theta)$ and every $z$ with $|\arg z|\le\sigma$, $\ \|\Gamma_z\|_1\le(\cos\sigma)^{-n/2}$;

(iii) for real $z=t>0$, $\Gamma_t$ is the heat kernel of [[def-heat-kernel]];

(iv) for every fixed $x$ the map $z\mapsto\Gamma_z(x)$ is holomorphic on $S_\theta$ with $\partial_z\Gamma_z(x)=\bigl(-\tfrac n{2z}+\tfrac{|x|^2}{4z^2}\bigr)\Gamma_z(x)$;

(v) for every compact $K\Subset S_\theta$ there are constants $c_K,C_K>0$ with $|\Gamma_z(x)|\le C_Ke^{-c_K|x|^2}$ and $|\partial_z\Gamma_z(x)|\le C_K(1+|x|^2)e^{-c_K|x|^2}$ for all $z\in K$, $x\in\mathbb R^n$.

Assume Countable Choice. Let $\theta\in(0,\pi/2)$ and $1\le p\le\infty$. For $z\in S_\theta$ and $f\in L^p(\mathbb R^n)$ define
$$H_zf:=\Gamma_z*f,$$
the convolution with the complex-time kernel of [[def-complex-time-heat-kernel-on-a-proper-sector]]. Then:

(i) $H_z$ is a bounded operator on $L^p(\mathbb R^n)$ with $\|H_z\|_{L^p\to L^p}\le(\cos\sigma)^{-n/2}$ whenever $|\arg z|\le\sigma<\theta$;

(ii) $H_zH_w=H_{z+w}$ whenever $z,w,z+w\in S_\theta$;

(iii) for every $f$ the map $z\mapsto H_zf$ is complex differentiable on $S_\theta$ in the norm of $L^p(\mathbb R^n)$, with derivative $(\partial_z\Gamma_z)*f$; consequently $z\mapsto H_z$ is holomorphic in operator norm on every proper subsector $S_\sigma$, $\sigma<\theta$.
